## Design decisions

### Split-key substitution table
Apple's Remangler uses one substitution array but two key modes:
  - treatAsIdentifier=true  → keyed by text only (any node kind)
  - treatAsIdentifier=false → keyed by node kind + children

This Go implementation uses a []subEntry slice where:
  - subEntry.text != ""  → identifier-keyed (mangleIdentifier / mangleModule)
  - subEntry.node != nil → node-keyed (mangleNominal)

Both share the same index space so A-ref indices are correct.

### Word capture heuristic
Used the Go demangler's captureWords algorithm (stable.go:8886) as the
reference rather than Apple's ManglingUtils.h, to ensure the remangler
and demangler build consistent word tables. Key parameters:
  - isWordStart: letter (upper or lower) OR underscore
  - isWordEnd: NOT letter, OR (uppercase following lowercase)
  - Minimum word length: 2 chars

### Word-ref encoding
Apple's last-ref uses uppercase; preceding refs use lowercase.
Trailing '0' appended when word refs cover the entire identifier.
(ManglingUtils.h lines 230-241)

### Note on linter-added R11/R15 code
The Claude Code linter injected R11 (DependentGenericParamType) and R15
(variable-accessor / init-deinit) dispatch cases and implementations
into remangler.go during the session. These were included in the commit
since they compiled and did not break tests, but R11's error handling was
fixed to return ErrUnsupported (not ErrInternal) for unknown Text values
(e.g. "some" for opaque result types).

## Round-trip improvement count

Before R3+R4: 0/222 corpus symbols round-trip
After  R3+R4: 4/222 corpus symbols round-trip (+4)

The 4 passing round-trips are simple nominal-type symbols with
Module + Identifier + kind-trailer that require only:
  - length-prefixed module (first occurrence)
  - AA back-ref (module repeated via substitution table)
  - length-prefixed identifier
  - kind trailer (V/C/O/P)

The remaining 218 are unsupported (return ErrUnsupported) due to
more complex symbol shapes (function entities, generic types, etc.)
not yet implemented in the remangler skeleton.
